/*!
    \class vsmm::ModListModel
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief List model with one row per installed mod.

    ModListModel is a flat list model over the mods of an \l vsmm::IModStore.
    Each row holds only a mod id. data() looks the mod up in the store on
    every call, so the model never keeps its own copy of mod data.

    The model is a QML singleton. \l vsmm::App passes the
    \l vsmm::ModStore to setStore() and sets the model as the source model of
    \l vsmm::ModSortFilterModel. After that the model follows the store
    signals. A \c modAdded signal appends a row at the end, \c modUpdated
    emits \c dataChanged() for the row of that mod, \c modRemoved removes the
    row, and \c modsReloading removes every row.

    QML reads the rows through the role names listed in \l Roles. See the
    \l [QML] {ModListModel} QML type for the role table seen from QML.

    \sa vsmm::ModSortFilterModel, vsmm::IModStore
*/

/*!
    \enum vsmm::ModListModel::Roles

    The data roles of the model. The QML role name of each value is given in
    parentheses.

    \value NameRole (\c modName) Display name of the mod.
    \value AuthorRole (\c modAuthor) List of the mod authors.
    \value VersionRole (\c modVersion) Installed version as a string.
    \value LatestVersionRole (\c modLatestVersion) Version of the available
           update as a string. Only meaningful when \c HasUpdateRole is
           \c true, otherwise \c 0.1.0.
    \value TagsRole (\c modTags) Tags from the online info.
    \value UrlRole (\c modUrl) Page of the mod on the mod database.
    \value SideRole (\c modSide) The \c side field of the online info, for example \c both.
    \value HasUpdateRole (\c modHasUpdate) \c true when an update is
           available.
    \value IconRole (\c modThumbnail) \c image://modicon URL of the mod
           icon, with the logo URL percent encoded in the \c url query item.
           Empty while the mod has no logo URL.
    \value IdRole (\c modId) Mod id.
    \value FavoriteRole (\c isFavoriteMod) \c true when the mod is a
           favorite.
    \value MarkedForUpdateRole (\c isMarkedForUpdate) \c true when the mod
           is marked for update.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModListModel::ModListModel(QObject *parent)

    Creates an empty model with the given \a parent. The model has no rows
    until setStore() is called and the store adds mods.
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModListModel::rowCount(const QModelIndex &parent) const
    \reimp

    Returns the number of mods in the model, or \c 0 for a valid parent.
*/

/*!
    \fn QVariant vsmm::ModListModel::data(const QModelIndex &index, int role) const
    \reimp

    Looks up the mod of the row in the store and returns the value for one of
    the \l Roles. Returns an invalid QVariant when the row or the mod is not
    found.
*/

/*!
    \fn QHash<int, QByteArray> vsmm::ModListModel::roleNames() const
    \reimp

    Returns the QML role names listed in \l Roles.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModListModel::setStore(vsmm::IModStore *store)

    Sets \a store as the source of the mods and connects to its
    \c modAdded, \c modUpdated, \c modsReloading and \c modRemoved signals.

    The store can be set only once. A second call logs a warning and does
    nothing. A null \a store is a fatal error. Call this before the model is
    used, because data() reads from the store.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModSortFilterModel
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Sorted and filtered proxy over vsmm::ModListModel.

    ModSortFilterModel sorts and filters \l vsmm::ModListModel. It is a QML
    singleton. \l vsmm::App sets the \l vsmm::ModListModel
    singleton as its source model.

    Rows are sorted by mod name, ascending and case insensitive. Sorting and
    filtering are dynamic, so rows are re-sorted, added and removed when the
    source data changes. The \l filterText property limits the rows to mods whose name
    contains the text.

    See the \l [QML] {ModSortFilterModel} QML type for the QML side.

    \sa vsmm::ModListModel
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::filterText
    \brief The text that the mod name of every accepted row contains.

    The match is case insensitive and checks only the mod name. Author, tags
    and id are not searched. An empty string accepts every row. The default is
    an empty string.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::ModSortFilterModel(QObject *parent)

    Creates the proxy with the given \a parent. Enables dynamic sorting and
    filtering and sorts column \c 0 in ascending order.
*/

/*!
    \fn QString vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::getFilterText() const

    Returns the current filter text.

    \sa filterText
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::setFilterText(const QString &filterText)

    Sets the filter text to \a filterText and filters the rows again. Does
    nothing when the text does not change. Emits filterTextChanged() after a
    change.

    \sa filterText
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::filterTextChanged()

    Emitted when \l filterText changes. Only QML bindings use this signal.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::lessThan(const QModelIndex &sourceLeft, const QModelIndex &sourceRight) const
    \reimp

    Compares the \l {vsmm::ModListModel::Roles}{NameRole} values of both rows,
    case insensitive.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModSortFilterModel::filterAcceptsRow(int sourceRow, const QModelIndex &sourceParent) const
    \reimp

    Accepts every row when \l filterText is empty. Otherwise accepts a row
    when its \l {vsmm::ModListModel::Roles}{NameRole} value contains the filter
    text, case insensitive.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModUpdateModel
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief List model with one row per mod of the current update batch.

    ModUpdateModel holds the progress of a mod update batch. It is a QML
    singleton. \l vsmm::App passes the \l vsmm::ModStore to
    setStore(), and the model then follows the update signals of the store.

    A \c modUpdateRequested signal starts a new batch. The model resets and
    adds one row for each requested mod that the store knows. Ids listed
    twice get one row. Each row keeps the mod name, the installed version and
    the version being installed, read from the store when the batch starts.
    The rows stay in the model after their mods finish, until clear() is
    called or the next batch starts.

    Each row moves through the \l State values. The progress signals of the
    store move a row from \c Queued to \c Downloading and update its
    download progress. \c modUpdateInstalling, \c modUpdateFinished and
    \c modUpdateFailed move it to \c Installing, \c Done and \c Failed.
    Signals for mods outside the batch, or for rows already \c Done or
    \c Failed, are ignored. When the store emits \c modsLoaded, every row
    that is not \c Done or \c Failed yet becomes \c Failed with the error
    text "Update ended without a result".

    The properties \l count, \l finishedCount, \l failedCount,
    \l totalProgress and \l active summarize the batch for QML. See the
    \l [QML] {ModUpdateModel} QML type for the role table seen from QML.

    \sa vsmm::IModStore
*/

/*!
    \enum vsmm::ModUpdateModel::Roles

    The data roles of the model. The QML role name of each value is given in
    parentheses.

    \value IdRole (\c modId) Mod id.
    \value NameRole (\c modName) Display name of the mod.
    \value FromVersionRole (\c fromVersion) Installed version when the batch
           started.
    \value ToVersionRole (\c toVersion) Version being installed.
    \value StateRole (\c updateState) Current \l State of the row.
    \value ProgressRole (\c progress) Progress of the row between \c 0 and
           \c 1. It is \c -1 while the row is \c Downloading and the download
           size is unknown.
    \value ErrorRole (\c errorText) Failure reason. Empty unless the state is
           \c Failed.
*/

/*!
    \enum vsmm::ModUpdateModel::State

    The state of one mod in the update batch.

    \value Queued No download progress has arrived yet. Progress is \c 0.
    \value Downloading The new zip is downloading.
    \value Installing The new zip is being installed. Progress is \c 1.
    \value Done The update finished. Progress is \c 1.
    \value Failed The update stopped. The \l {vsmm::ModUpdateModel::Roles}{ErrorRole}
           value holds the reason.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModUpdateModel::count
    \brief The number of mods in the batch.

    The value changes when a batch starts and when clear() removes the rows.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModUpdateModel::finishedCount
    \brief The number of mods in the \c Done or \c Failed state.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModUpdateModel::failedCount
    \brief The number of mods in the \c Failed state.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModUpdateModel::totalProgress
    \brief The progress of the whole batch between \c 0 and \c 1.

    Rows in the \c Done or \c Failed state count as complete. A download with
    an unknown size counts as \c 0. The value is \c 0 when the batch is
    empty.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModUpdateModel::active
    \brief Whether at least one mod of the batch is not \c Done or \c Failed.

    The value is \c false when the batch is empty.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModUpdateModel::ModUpdateModel(QObject *parent)

    Creates an empty model with the given \a parent.
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModUpdateModel::rowCount(const QModelIndex &parent) const
    \reimp

    Returns the number of mods in the batch, or \c 0 for a valid parent.
*/

/*!
    \fn QVariant vsmm::ModUpdateModel::data(const QModelIndex &index, int role) const
    \reimp

    Returns the value of the row for one of the \l Roles, or an invalid
    QVariant for an unknown row or role.
*/

/*!
    \fn QHash<int, QByteArray> vsmm::ModUpdateModel::roleNames() const
    \reimp

    Returns the QML role names listed in \l Roles.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModUpdateModel::setStore(vsmm::IModStore *store)

    Sets \a store as the source of the update batches and connects to its
    \c modUpdateRequested, \c modUpdateProgress, \c modUpdateInstalling,
    \c modUpdateFinished, \c modUpdateFailed and \c modsLoaded signals.

    The store can be set only once. A second call logs a warning and does
    nothing. A null \a store is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModUpdateModel::count() const

    Returns the number of mods in the batch.
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModUpdateModel::finishedCount() const

    Returns the number of mods in the \c Done or \c Failed state.
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModUpdateModel::failedCount() const

    Returns the number of mods in the \c Failed state.
*/

/*!
    \fn double vsmm::ModUpdateModel::totalProgress() const

    Returns the progress of the whole batch between \c 0 and \c 1.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModUpdateModel::isActive() const

    Returns \c true while at least one mod of the batch is not \c Done or
    \c Failed.

    \sa active
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModUpdateModel::clear()

    Removes all rows of a finished batch and emits countChanged() and
    progressChanged(). Logs a warning and does nothing while \l active is
    \c true. Does nothing when the model is empty.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModUpdateModel::countChanged()

    Emitted when \l count changes, that is when a batch starts or clear()
    removes the rows. Only QML bindings use this signal.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModUpdateModel::progressChanged()

    Emitted when \l finishedCount, \l failedCount, \l totalProgress or
    \l active can have changed. This happens when a batch starts, on every
    download progress step, on every state change and in clear(). Only QML
    bindings use this signal.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModImageProvider
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Asynchronous QML image provider for mod icons.

    ModImageProvider serves the mod icons that QML requests. \c App creates it,
    calls setHttpClient(), and adds it to the QML engine under the name
    \c modicon. \c App also connects the \c modsReloading and \c modRemoved
    signals of the \l vsmm::ModStore to onModsReloading() and onModRemoved().

    An image id has the form \c {<modId>?url=<percent encoded logo url>}.
    The \l {vsmm::ModListModel::Roles}{IconRole} of \l vsmm::ModListModel returns
    URLs in this form, already percent encoded.

    The provider downloads an icon through the \l vsmm::IHttpClient the
    first time a mod id is requested. Requests for the same mod id that
    arrive while the download runs wait for the same download. Images are
    decoded on a separate thread pool and kept in an in-memory cache of up
    to 32 MiB, keyed by mod id. When the downloaded data is not a valid
    image, the provider remembers that the mod has no icon and answers later
    requests with an error until the mods reload or the mod is removed. A
    failed download is not remembered, so the next request downloads again.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModImageProvider::ModImageProvider()

    Creates the provider. Call setHttpClient() before the first image
    request.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModImageProvider::~ModImageProvider()

    Destroys the provider after waiting for all running image decodes to
    finish.
*/

/*!
    \fn QQuickImageResponse *vsmm::ModImageProvider::requestImageResponse(const QString &id, const QSize &requestedSize)
    \reimp

    Returns a response that resolves from the cache, with an error for a mod
    without an icon, or after the download finishes. With a valid requested
    size, the image is scaled to it, and the aspect ratio is ignored only
    when both dimensions are below 100 pixels.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModImageProvider::setHttpClient(vsmm::IHttpClient *httpClient)

    Sets \a httpClient as the client used to download icons. The client can
    be set only once. A second call logs a warning and does nothing. A null
    \a httpClient is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModImageProvider::imageDownloaded(QString id, QImage image, QString error)

    Emitted when the download of the icon of mod \a id ends. On success
    \a image holds the decoded icon and \a error is empty. On failure
    \a image is null and \a error holds the reason. The pending responses
    for that mod resolve from this signal. It can be emitted from a decode
    thread.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModImageProvider::onModsReloading()

    Clears the image cache and the list of mods without an icon, so every
    icon downloads again on its next request.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModImageProvider::onModRemoved(QStringView modId)

    Removes the cached image of mod \a modId and forgets that the mod had no
    icon.
*/
